/E (ownerKey: The public key of the owner of the document.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The issuerKey and ownerKey are used to verify the authenticity of the document and the signature. The issuerKey is used to verify the signature of the document, while the ownerKey is used to verify the signature of the token. With the presence of the issuerKey and ownerKey, the verifier can verify the authenticity of a token without relying on network connections.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
